\subsection{3-designs from conference matrices}
In this subsection, we show how $3$-designs can be obtained from symmetric conference matrices, skew-symmetric conference matrices, and skew Hadamard matrices.  

A \textbf{symmetric (resp.\ skew-symmetric) Seidel matrix} is a $\{0,\pm 1\}$-matrix $S$ with zero diagonal and all off-diagonal entries non-zero such that $S=S^\transpose$ (resp.\ $S=-S^\transpose$).
 A \textbf{conference matrix} is a Seidel matrix $S$ of order $n$ such that $SS^\transpose = (n-1)I$.
Using \cite[Table 4.1]{vLS}, one can obtain Table~\ref{tab:detSeidel34}, which lists $k \times k$ principal minors of a symmetric Seidel matrix. 
