By \cite[Theorem 2]{RB72}, the existence of doubly regular tournaments of order $n$ is equivalent to that of so-called \textit{skew Hadamard matrices} of order $n+1$.
Note that $H$ is a skew Hadamard matrix if and only if $H-I$ is a skew-conference matrix.   
We refer again the reader to \cite[Section 9.3.1]{SY} for further details on the existence of skew Hadamard matrices.

