A viable family has emerged from Section 2.2, and it clears the Step‑0 distinction honestly as Track B. Each instance asks for exact block counts in several transformed Paley conference-matrix hypergraphs. Exhaustive principal-minor classification is polynomial but costs millions of 4×4 tests at the planned preset; Theorem 2.2 plus Examples 2.3–2.4 compress the work to roughly eight integer operations per record. I’m benchmarking that gap now and will reject it if the “compact” side proves comparably mechanical or the hinted oracle dissolves it.
